Lancashire partners,

Please find below the Lancashire Resilience Forum situation report for Storm Fenella response.

Report no.   | 6
Date/time    | 15 January 2026, 19:00
Status       | Major incident declared. Response phase.
Coastal      | Overtopping at high tide on the Morecambe frontage. Next high tide 0942.
Responding   | Network Rail, Environment Agency, Electricity NW, Lancashire County Council

Locations:
  * West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): reopened (run by Network Rail)
  * Carnforth Primary Substation: flooded, out of service
  * A683 near Hornby: remains closed (flooding) (run by Lancashire CC)
  * West End Community Centre: rest centre OPEN (run by Lancaster City Council)

Next update to follow after the TCG.

